are you serious dude what'd i get right  everything hey guys it's vadim with max  tech and today i am a happy guy  because apple has finally redesigned  their imac  and i actually got quite a few of the  predictions from yesterday's video  correct and i'm pretty sure that i was  the only one in the tech space  who thought that the chin might actually  stick around but anyway in this video  i'm gonna go through everything new with  the apple silicon imac i'm gonna talk  about what i got wrong and what i got  right  and then i'm gonna talk about when we  should be expecting the larger imac  with the m1x chip so let's get right  into it  starting from the top the imac looks  great in seven  different colors which john prosser  basically nailed with that leak  it's also incredibly thin precisely just  11.5 millimeters thick which is  surprisingly  even thinner than just the bottom half  of the macbook pro  which is mind-blowing and if you're  wondering how apple achieved this  i explained it in yesterday's prediction  video where i mentioned that basically  everything would be soldered onto the  main logic board  drastically reducing the size since  there's not going to be discrete  graphics in all of the other components  needed for the power hungry intel chips  and the crazy part was that they were  able to fit it all  behind the chin which i'm glad i was  right about the only detail i got wrong  was that i thought it would be  drastically thinner  and i wasn't expecting them to remove  the apple logo  or cover the entire front with a single  sheet of glass  which honestly looks amazing and another  thing i didn't expect at all was that  apple would take the power supply  out of the body and connect it to the  all new  color matched and braided power cable  and wow that magnetic connection feature  is definitely hinting at maxsafe coming  to the redesigned macbooks  and it's awesome that they were able to  pack a gigabit ethernet port into the  brick  as an upgrade option from the base model  i'm also glad that my prediction that  the m1x chip wasn't ready was correct  even though i said there was a small  chance that we could see it happen  but it looks like we're sticking with  just the m1 ship  on this imac another prediction i made  was that the imac would pack in  a fan but apple actually put in two of  them  which is a bit surprising but i'm glad  to hear that it'll be a whisper quiet  10 decibels under typical use this means  that both of the fans will always be  running  just like the current m1 mac mini does  right now the only difference is that  apple probably  redesigned the fans to make them super  quiet at idle speed  another shocker was when apple claimed  that the new six speaker system on this  imac  has better speakers than any mac ever  which is surprising because the speakers  on my current imac pro  are incredible but with two subwoofers  that cancel out each other's vibrations  along with a dedicated tweeter  on each side i totally believe that the  sound quality is going to be incredible  so if you want to see comparison to the  current imac pro  speakers which are the best speakers out  of any mac  click the subscribe button below so you  don't miss out as far as the stand it's  now squared off  which basically everyone was expecting  and of course  it's permanently attached to the imac  just like we thought it would be  and it's nice to hear that you can still  order an imac with a vase amount adapter  instead of the stand now as far as the  ports i got them  completely wrong i thought that we'd  basically have the same ports as the  21.5 inch imac  with the sd card slot and usb a ports  but apple chose to go with up to four  usbc ports  with just two of them supporting  thunderbolt as well as a headphone jack  on the side  which is very convenient it's also very  interesting that the base model only  gets  two thunderbolt ports which requires a  totally  different motherboard compared to the  more expensive models  so it looks like my theory on why there  were two leaked imac  identifiers within beta code turned out  to be right  as far as the display the 24 inch size  leaks were correct and i  am extremely happy that my 4.5 k  display resolution prediction was  correct since 5k  is definitely overkill for a 24 inch  display  so i based my prediction on apple  hitting a target of 218  pixels per inch which they did with 4.5  k resolution  except for some reason i totally messed  up and i thought that it would have a 16  by 10 aspect ratio  but at least i got the 4480 horizontal  pixel count spot on  another prediction i got right was the  1080p facetime camera  and because of the m1 chip it should  look incredible  with new software features added thanks  to the new neural engine  and something that surprised me was that  they said  that this imac will have the best  microphone system in any mac  using a three microphone array with  beamforming  and yesterday's video i also claimed  that apple would color match the  keyboard and the mouse  to the imac body color that you choose  so i'm glad that i was right  but man there are gonna be a lot of  different skus  however one thing that i got totally  wrong  was that i did not believe that apple  would be able to get touch id  into the magic keyboard since it would  require your sensitive data  to travel to the imac wirelessly but i  guess that apple was able to figure it  out  i personally thought that they would go  with face id instead  since we had some leaks within macos  beta code but i guess we're gonna have  to wait and see  for maybe larger imacs or the redesigned  macbooks to get face id  now one prediction from yesterday's  video that i got totally spot on  was the starting price of thirteen  hundred dollars  and the reason i thought that was  because that was the price of the retina  4k  21.5 inch model which this new one  directly replaces and yes people are  gonna gladly cough up  thirteen hundred dollars for an m1 chip  powered imac  because of the amazing new redesign  just like i said in yesterday's video  and if you think about it the m1 chip is  already amazing  with an 85 faster cpu than the 21.5 inch  imac models  and a gpu that's 50 faster  than the best vega 20 discrete graphics  option  in some real world we're close and  because it's got the same m1 chip  we have the exact same 8 gigs of ram and  256 gigs of ssd storage  at the base price and up to 16 gigs of  ram  and 2 terabytes of storage which  perfectly matches the options  on the m1 mac mini just as we expected  however there are a couple of  disappointments so let's get right into  those  first off we can't order it until the  last date of this month and it won't  even  ship until the second half of may which  is a huge bummer because we want them  right now  and the second disappointment is the  fact that the base model only gets a 7  core gpu  but it's not that big of a deal because  in our testing with a thermal pad  modded base macbook air the 7 core gpu  wasn't that much slower  than the macbook pros 8 core but i'd say  that the  even bigger disappointment is not  getting the extra two usbc  ports on the base model as well as not  getting the ethernet port  on the power supply that's included and  we also shouldn't be surprised that it  only  officially supports one external display  since that's a limitation with the m1  chip but on the plus side  you do get a usbc to lightning cable in  the box for charging the mouse  compared to the old usb a version now  here's a really interesting detail that  i just noticed  the 24 inch imac comes with 143 watt  power adapter  which is absolutely overkill for the m1  imac  even with the 4.5 k display so because  of that i believe that apple created  this  power adapter with the larger future  imac in mind  so they only have one power adapter for  all of the redesigned imac models  so with that let's finish off this video  with my predictions for the larger imac  that we're expecting to come later this  year i personally have a pretty good  feeling that it's actually going to be  called  the imac pro so the 24 inch imac  will be the only regular imac model and  we're going to have a 30 to 32 inch imac  pro as a replacement for the 27 inch  imac  because of that i believe that the imac  pro is going to be coming this december  since that's when the previous imac pro  and the mac pros  were always released on top of that  it'll most likely come with a chin  since apple kept it for the 24 inch  model but i definitely think that the  overall body size and thickness is not  going to be  nearly as thin because it's going to  need a more powerful cooling system  but i have a good feeling that apple is  gonna reuse the same exact 1080p webcam  the same exact speaker system and the  microphone system as well  but as far as all of the crazy colors i  do not think that the imac pro is  getting those color options  they're gonna keep it very subtle and  neutral like they always do for their  pro  products so probably just space gray or  space black  or maybe even a silver option it's  almost certainly gonna come with a 6k  display and it'll come with the m1x chip  at the base price  the same one that's going to be coming  in the macbook pros  but it's also going to have an option  for an even better chip  potentially the m1z as well as one or  two  dedicated gpu options and in terms of  the pricing i think the apple is going  to be going with a 3 000  starting price for the base model which  is a good middle ground  between the 27 inch imac and the imac  pro  retail prices but i do want to let you  know that it's way too early to know any  of this stuff for sure  but if you enjoyed my predictions for  the 24 inch imac  then definitely click the circle about  to subscribe because we're going to be  getting our hands on those next month  and testing them out and you don't want  to miss it so thanks for watching and  we'll see you in  the next video

